// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/course/course.t27 -- the t27 course: from zero to a program on a real FPGA
; Source of truth for apps/website/scripts/course-from-spec.mjs (gHashTag/trinity), which
; compiles this file with the vendored compiler (public/t27/t27_compiler.wasm), checks the
; constant schema, evaluates every test block below, checks that every widget a lesson names
; is in specs/widgets/gallery.t27 and that every gallery widget is used by some lesson of some
; course, compiles every lesson spec and refuses one that is not clean, checks the Russian
; bundle named by specs/course/course-ru.t27, and only then writes src/lib/course.generated.ts
; (the page at #/course) and a byte-identical copy of this file at public/learn/course.t27.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN). The Russian words live in the bundle.

; WHAT THE COURSE IS: course 1 of specs/course/courses.t27, 27 lessons in 9 modules of 3, for a
; reader who has never written for a chip: what an FPGA is, how numbers become bits, a t27 spec
; of your own, how t27c compiles it, and how it becomes a bitstream on a real board. Each lesson
; is a short text, one working widget from the gallery, one t27 spec the reader runs in the
; player, and one thing to try in both. The widgets are not drawn for the course: they are the
; same tools a hardware engineer uses on t27.ai, built from real runs of t27c, yosys, nextpnr and
; openFPGALoader on our bench. Course 2, AI numbers (specs/course/ai-numbers.t27), starts where
; this one ends, and its last lesson's page links there.

; WHAT THE COURSE DOES NOT DO: it says no number of its own. A number a lesson needs is on the
; widget or in the spec, which names where it came from. The one exception is the t27b figure in
; lesson 12, quoted with its denominator and the run that produced it.

; WHY 27: 3 cubed lessons, the size of a TRI-27 word. Changing the shape changes the tests.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module course;

pub const KIND : str = "course";
pub const ID : str = "course";
pub const SCHEMA_VERSION : u8 = 1;
